      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-03-06_WidnesExaminer_art0006" n="art0006">
        <head>BIirrILTREAnY, MARCEI ta,, 190 S.</head>
        <p>BIirrILTREAnY, MARCEI ta,, 190 S.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON INFIRMARY AND DISPENSARY.—NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the Annual General Meeting of the Governors of the Warrington Infirmary and Dispensary will be held in the Council Chamber of the Town Hall, Warrington on Tuesday, the 23rd day of March, 1909, at three o'clock in the afternoon.</p>
        <p>The Board of Management invite applications for the appointment of an Honorary Assistant Surgeon. Candidates must be registered to practise Medicine and Surgery. No medical gentleman is eligible unless be has practiced within the County Borough of Warrington for one year.</p>
        <p>Rules end Duties may be had on application. Applications for the post, without testimonials to be sent to the Secretary on or before Saturday, March 20th, 1909. Canvassing will disqualify. J. H. J. HAMPSON, Secretary.</p>
        <p>In the matter of the Companies Acts, 1862 to 1907, and in the Matter of The NEW SALT SYNDICATE, LIMITED (in Voluntary Liquidation.) NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN pursuant to Section 27 of the Companies Act, 1907, that a MEETING of the CREDITORS of the above named Company will be held at the office of Messrs. Fitzpatrick, Graham, Greenwood and Co., 147, Leadenhall Street in the City of London at 12 o'clock noon, on Monday, the 15th day of March, 1909. Any person claiming to be a Creditor and wishing to be present should at once inform the undersigned at his address, 147, Leadenhall et., aforesaid. Dated this 26th day of February. 1909. J.FITZPATRICK, Liquidator. WINTER ASSIZES, -3H, 1909.</p>
        <p>LIVERPOOL MAE</p>
        <p>The Commissions for holding these Assizes will be opened at Liverpool, on MONDAY, the Bth March. The Court will sit on TUESDAY, the 9th March, at 11 o'clock a.m., and on every other day during the Assizes at 10.30 o'clock a.m., unless otherwise directed. The Prosecution and Witnesses in the after-mentioned cases are required to be in attendance at the times specified in the following List, and not earlier: and on all subsequent days, at the sitting of the Court; and the trials are to proceed in the order in which the cases are arranged in the List, unless the Court shall otherwise direct, viz. :</p>
        <p>On TUESDAY, the 9th March, at 11 o'clock a.m. - The King versus John Fairclough and another, steal- ing a post letter; Sam Lee, murder; John Thompson, forgery ; Emma Swindells, murder ; William Ferry, false pretences ; Richard Reid, criminal assault ; Louis Henshall, forgery; John Powell and another, shopbreaking ; William Jones, criminal assault' - Thomas Murray, criminal assault; William McCormick, murder; John Beer, burglary; William Hill, larcency ; Sarah Elizabeth Taylor, cencealment of birth; Isaac Crawshaw, wounding; Timothy O'Neill, larcencv • Thomas Leicester and another, housebreaking; John Costello, criminal assault ; Patrick Doolan, robbery; Dennis Smith, mnrder.</p>
        <p>In the Mat tor of the Companies Acts, 1862 to 1907, and of the -NEW SALT SYNDICATE, LIMITED, (in Voluntary Liquidation). _ _ _</p>
        <p>IN-OTI.CE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the Creditors of the above named Company are required, on or before Monday the 12th day of April, 1909, to send their names and addresses and the particulars of their debts or claims, and the names and addresses of their solicitors (if any), to James Fitzpatrick, Chartered Accountant, 147 Leadenhall Street In the City of Lon- don, E.C., the Liquidator of the said Company ; and, if so required by notice in writing by the said Liquidator, are, by their Solicitors, or personally, to come in and prove their said debts or claims at such time and place as shall be specified in such notice, or in default thereof they will be excluded from the benefit of any distribu- tion made before such debts are proved. • Dated, this 26th day of February, 1909. J. FITZPATRICK, Liquidator.</p>
