      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-03-06_WidnesExaminer_art0101" n="art0101">
        <head>WARRINGTON TOWN COUNCIL.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON TOWN COUNCIL.</p>
        <p>A Costly Clerical Error.</p>
        <p>There were numerous contentious matters on the agenda for the monthly meeting of the Warrington Town Council on Tuesday evening and over two hours Were occupied in the transaction of the business. The Mayor (Alderman Forshaw) presided, and there were also present:—The Deputy Mayor(Alderman Smethurst), Aldermen A. Bennett, W. Bolton, T. Burton, L. Ellison, John Evans, D. Tinnion, Councillors T. H. Ashcroft, T. Barton, T. Birtles, J. Broadhurst, T. Chantler, J. G. Craik, James Evans, J. Hawthorn, Dr. Joseph, F. T. Lashford, Lord, .1. Pemberton, W. B. Roberts, W. Rogers, .1. Sankey, IP Singleton, J. Skelland, J. Fulton- Smith, 0. Toole, J. Wilkinson, W. J. Wilson, Messrs. J. clerk L. Whittle (town clerk), A. T. Hallaway (deputy town th), J. Fairhurst (borough treasurer), T. Longdin .I!!orough surveyor), .1. Dees (water engineer), C. adeley (librarian), W. S. Haddock (gas engineer), F. V. L. Matthias (electrical engineer), J. M. Murray (director of education), .Dr. J. C. Hibbert (medical °Meer).</p>
